                <pb facs="0505" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2231/173a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gonzalez</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-17T14:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1937—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Consul General at Guayaquil reports extensive changes in Ecuadoran import
                    tariff effective July 5.</p>
                <p>These changes should be considered before you present the list enclosed with the
                    Department’s instruction No. 244 of July 10.<anchor n="40" xml:id="d507-f1"/>
                    Keep the Department informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
